  "database": "schemabench_0101",
  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0101 database contains four tables: Data, Metadata - Countries, Metadata - Indicators, and target. The Data table contains information on the values of various indicators for different countries over the years 1960 to 2012. Each row in the table represents a specific country and indicator combination, with columns for the country name, country code, indicator name, indicator code, and the values for each year. The table has a primary key composed of the country code and indicator code, and foreign keys to the Metadata - Countries and Metadata - Indicators tables. The Metadata - Countries table contains information on the countries, including their names, codes, regions, income groups, and special notes. The Metadata - Indicators table contains information on the indicators, including their names, codes, source notes, and source organizations. The target table contains the values of the indicators for the year 2012, with a foreign key to the Metadata - Countries table.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a predictive analytics system to estimate \"Forest area (% of land area)\" for 247 countries in 2012. The estimation is based on historical data ranging from 1960 to 2011. The data is stored in a structured database format.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- Accurately predict the percentage of forest area for each specified country in 2012.\n- Utilize historical data from 1960 to 2011 for prediction.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Environmental analysts who will use the predictions for research and policy-making.\n- Data scientists responsible for developing and refining the prediction model.\n- Government agencies interested in monitoring and managing forest resources.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Extract and preprocess historical data from the database.\n- Develop a predictive model using machine learning techniques to estimate 2012 forest area percentages based on past data.\n- Validate and evaluate the model's accuracy with appropriate metrics.\n- Provide a user interface for analysts to access predictions and assess data.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ensure data security and integrity throughout the data processing pipeline.\n- Design the system to handle up to 500 concurrent users querying the predictions.\n- Deliver predictions with a latency of no more than 2 seconds per request.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0101.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0101\nCREATE TABLE `data` (\n  `country_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `indicator_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `country_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `indicator_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `value_1960` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1961` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1962` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1963` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1964` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1965` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1966` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1967` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1968` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1969` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1970` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1971` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1972` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1973` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1974` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1975` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1976` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1977` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1978` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1979` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1980` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1981` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1982` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1983` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1984` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1985` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1986` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1987` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1988` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1989` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1990` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1991` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1992` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1993` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1994` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1995` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1996` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1997` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1998` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_1999` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2000` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2001` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2002` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2003` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2004` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2005` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2006` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2007` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2008` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2009` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2010` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2011` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `value_2012` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_code`, `indicator_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `data_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`country_code`) REFERENCES `metadata_countries` (`country_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `data_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`indicator_code`) REFERENCES `metadata_indicators` (`indicator_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `metadata_countries` (\n  `country_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `country_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `region` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `income_group` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `special_notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `metadata_indicators` (\n  `indicator_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `indicator_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `source_notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `source_organization` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`indicator_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `target` (\n  `country_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `indicator_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `value_2012` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_code`, `indicator_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `target_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`country_code`) REFERENCES `metadata_countries` (`country_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
